      "title": "Radiation sets the stack height",
      "description": "A flare safely burns gas released by relief valves and blowdown. Its height and location are set so thermal radiation at grade stays within limits (e.g. ≈ 1.58 kW/m² for continuous exposure of personnel, higher for short emergency exposure — API 521, verify edition). Steam (or air) injected at the tip mixes air into the flame for smokeless burning; continuous pilots guarantee ignition; the water seal and purge gas with a molecular seal stop air entering and flashback.",
